{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AJjjChk3pcrbAXCeheMtD8","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found information about the KIP-1312 decision on the record type, but I need to clarify what the sources show:\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\nAccording to the **pull-requests.md** file, the decision for KIP-1312 (Support unregistering controllers) was to **create a new dedicated record type** called `UnregisterControllerRecord` rather than reuse an existing record type. This is documented in PR #22191:\\\\n\\\\n**Citation from pull-requests.md (line 4716):**\\\\n- `UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record schema + new MetadataVersion IBP_4_4_IV2\\\\n\\\\nThe PR summary shows that the implementation includes:\\\\n- `UnregisterControllerRequest` and `UnregisterControllerResponse` RPC schemas  \\\\n- `Admin#unregisterController` interface via AdminClient\\\\n- **`UnregisterControllerRecord` metadata record schema** + new MetadataVersion IBP_4_4_IV2\\\\n- Controller-side handling and metadata updates\\\\n- CLI commands and admin tooling\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:** **pull-requests.md** (lines 4706-4722)\\\\n\\\\nHowever, I was unable to locate the detailed KIP discussion documentation that shows Jun Rao's specific questions about whether to reuse an existing record type or create a new one, or Kevin Wu's response justifying this decision. The discussion threads are referenced in **discussions.md** but the detailed technical reasoning for this specific design choice does not appear to be captured in the available context.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"discussions.md\\\",\\\"index.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":77.17,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":3,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":867363,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":54904,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.22664030000000002,\\\"input_tokens\\\":266,\\\"output_tokens\\\":5966}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_us